From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: flip/rotate of every orientation, narrow and wide format conversions

IWICBitmapFlipRotator only handled the unrotated orientations and copied the
rows of the others wrongly. CopyPixels now maps each destination pixel back to
its source (rotate clockwise first, then flip in the destination), validates
the rectangle, stride and buffer, and works for every bit depth including the
sub-byte formats and rectangles that start inside a byte.

The format converter gained the destinations that were missing: 1, 2 and 4 bit
palette formats (nearest palette entry), BlackWhite, 2 and 4 bit gray, 16 bit
gray, BGR555, BGR565 and 48bppRGB, plus the sources 32bppRGB, 32bppPRGBA,
32bppGrayFloat and the narrow gray formats for the existing destinations. The
wide sources and destinations go through one 16 bit per channel path. Generated
predefined palettes with more colours than the destination holds are rejected.
